From 4db3c428c5243233d3f38a4399615386302fd988 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forum_service <forum_service@sophgo.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 17:27:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] build: generate the edge partitions from the partition xml
 and support 64bit cimg

- partition_emmc.xml of edge_ubuntu_emmc_ainas : the layout(BOOT/RECOVERY/
  MISC/ROOTFS/ROOTFS_RW/DATA) and the offsets are the same as the ones of
  partition32G_sector.xml, the reserved area of the partition table is
  described by the "GPT" row.

- common_functions.sh : new pack_edge_*() generate the images of the edge
  (ubuntu/debian) partitions from $FLASH_PARTITION_XML : the file system is
  created as large as the content needs, shrunk with resize2fs -M and packed
  as a cimg image. pack_gpt() does not remove the "GPT" row from the xml
  anymore, mk_gpt() handles it.

- envsetup_soc.sh : call pack_edge_*()/pack_gpt() for the ubuntu/debian rootfs.

- mk_gpt.c : the "GPT" row describes the reserved area in front of the first
  partition(first lba) and DATA takes the rest of the total size, limited by
  last_usable_lba. Otherwise the last partition is out of the usable range of
  the gpt and tools like sgdisk/parted refuse to update the table, so the
  resize-helper of the target can not grow DATA to the end of the emmc.

- raw2cimg.py/raw2cimg_edge.py : the file size of the container header and the
  offset/part size of the chunk header are low/high 32bit pairs plus a large
  file flag, so an image larger than 4GiB and a partition behind the first
  4GiB of the emmc can be programmed. The default gpt part is only added when
  the xml does not describe it.

- XmlParser.py : an empty size_in_kb means "not specified".

